     1	# Generalization campaign: three-dataset response assessment of the frozen pipeline
     2	
     3	Branch `generalization/campaign-1` · frozen baseline tag `frozen-2026-08-01` ·
     4	deadline AAS 249 regular abstract Tue 2026-09-30.
     5	
     6	## Claim under test
     7	
     8	The 2026-08-01 ZTF white-dwarf run showed the variance census and the blind
     9	Lomb-Scargle search have complementary selection functions — but on 19
    10	truth-labeled stars, with a known mechanism, and injections conditioned on two
    11	light curves. Red-team verdict: NO-GO as a discovery claim. The flip condition:
    12	run the *frozen* pipeline on externally labeled samples large enough to
    13	measure class-specific response rates with uncertainty.
    14	
    15	G1 review (sol ×3, 2026-08-28) sharpened what this campaign can honestly
    16	claim — THREE SEPARATE response assessments, never pooled into one
    17	"selection function":
    18	- D1: the anchor (19 labeled WDs + 928-star catalog, published);
    19	- D2: conditional injection-recovery efficiency of the frozen search stage
    20	  (TESS-truth signals in real ZTF windows) — labeled as such, NOT real-sky
    21	  completeness and NOT an independently labeled sample;
    22	- D3: externally labeled, magnitude-restricted validation on real ZTF
    23	  photometry (detection completeness, frequency recovery, negative-class
    24	  trigger rate).
    25	Banned phrases (G1): "quantified selection-function measurement", "real-sky
    26	completeness" (for D2), "D3 FPR", unqualified "purity". Estimand names in
    27	METRICS_SPEC.md are binding.
    28	
    29	## Frozen-core / adapter-shell architecture
    30	
    31	- Tag `frozen-2026-08-01` = branch point. Zero edits to any script that
    32	  produced the published bundle; the referee check is an empty
    33	  `git diff frozen-2026-08-01 -- scripts/<frozen five>`.
    34	- Frozen five: `run_catalog_lomb_scargle.py`, `run_lomb_scargle.py`,
    35	  `lomb_scargle_common.py`, `build_catalog_panels.py`,
    36	  `fetch_catalog_lightcurves.py`. SHA-256 pinned in
    37	  `scripts/generalization/frozen_api.py`; `assert_frozen()` runs at import and
    38	  at the top of every campaign script.
    39	- Campaign code lives in `scripts/generalization/` and imports the frozen
    40	  callables only through `frozen_api`. The frozen CLI never runs on campaign
    41	  data (its `main()` merges the WD roster and rewrites the published table);
    42	  `verify_cli_identity.py` proves the import path is byte-identical to the
    43	  CLI's internal call path.
    44	- Known frozen quirks are pinned by `tests/test_frozen_constants.py`, fixed by
    45	  nothing: the `>= 2.5` vs `> 2.5` census inconsistency (provably
    46	  non-affecting: 0 of 5,568 published ratios within 1e-4 of 2.5; campaign
    47	  metrics use `>=` and assert no campaign ratio equals 2.5 exactly), the
    48	  bootstrap's `int(source_id[-9:])` seed (harmless for 19-digit numeric
    49	  campaign ids by construction), duplicated pass-bound literals (AST-scan
    50	  test).
    51	
    52	### Campaign source_id convention
    53	
    54	19-digit numeric strings: `90…` D3 targets, `92…` D2 arm B, `93…` D2 arm A,
    55	`94…` D2 Gaussian nulls, `95…` D2 paired real-window controls. No collision
    56	with Gaia DR3 ids; always valid for the frozen seed convention.
    57	
    58	### Replay gate (blocks everything)
    59	
    60	`replay_gate.py` re-runs the frozen `analyze_star` through `frozen_api` on 25
    61	published stars (all 7 schema-v2 + 18 stride-sampled schema-v1) and
    62	byte-compares against the committed bundle. Comparison tiers: raw-identical;
    63	identical after CRLF→LF normalization (git stored the bundle normalized);
    64	identical after the documented v1→v2 schema transform — 921/928 published
    65	files were written before commit `fa16d7f` (parent `e917bd1`), which added
    66	sparse-input early-exit branches plus the `available`/`unavailable_reason`
    67	keys and bumped `schema_version` 1→2. For any star that yields candidates,
    68	the numeric path is unchanged (the new branches fire only on sparse inputs
    69	that previously crashed; all 7 v2 records exercise exactly those branches).
    70	The downgrade transform removes only the two added keys and byte-compares
    71	everything retained. Gate passes only with a nonempty roster, zero
    72	mismatches AND at least one schema-v2 star reproducing with no transform
    73	(unconditional). VERDICT 2026-08-28 (jacks-7i-5090, production venv):
    74	PASS — 7 identical_newline + 18 identical_v1_schema, 25/25.
    75	Campaign L-S runs are valid only on machine+env pairs that passed the gate;
    76	`run_generalization_ls.py` refuses to start without a matching PASS
    77	attestation (env fingerprint + frozen SHAs). Planned W2 hardening: one full
    78	928-star replay on the production machine as the definitive baseline, and a
    79	panel-stage golden replay (shard rebuild byte-compare incl. bjd_tdb, IERS
    80	auto-download disabled).
    81	
    82	### Environment
    83	
    84	The published run's venv (laptop `jacks-7i-5090`) is recorded in
    85	`generalization/env/FROZEN_ENV.md`; the numerics-bearing subset is pinned in
    86	`requirements-frozen.txt` (Python 3.12.12, numpy 2.3.x, scipy 1.16.3, astropy
    87	8.0.1, iers-data 0.2026.7.27, pyerfa 2.0.1.5, pandas 2.3.3). Discrepancy on
    88	record: pip metadata said numpy 2.3.3 but the venv imports 2.3.5; the replay
    89	gate verdict on that venv is the authority on whether the published numbers
    90	reproduce under what is actually installed. requirements-frozen.txt is updated
    91	to whatever passes the gate, and the manifest of every campaign run records
    92	`env_versions()` at runtime.
    93	
    94	## D1 — ZTF white dwarfs (anchor, done)
    95	
    96	The published 2026-08-01 bundle: 19-star truth roster + 928-star catalog.
    97	No re-run; campaign metrics re-read the published per-star JSONs.
    98	
    99	## D3 — ZTF × Kepler delta Scuti (real ZTF light curves, external labels)
   100	
   101	- Labels: Murphy+2019 (VizieR J/MNRAS/485/2380/table1, 14,330 Kepler A/F
   102	  stars; `dSct` flag 0/1/2 — ships its own labeled negative class).
   103	- Amplitude axis: Mo+2026 (J/A+A/710/A245): table2 = 259,883 extracted
   104	  frequencies (SNR>8) for 1,838 delta Scutis → per-star dominant amplitude
   105	  (ppt × 1.0857 → mmag); table1 = confirmed super-Nyquist modes → the
   106	  sub-hour stratum (any confirmed SNF ⇒ real mode above Kepler LC Nyquist
   107	  283.2 µHz ⇒ P < 59 min). This replaces the originally scouted Bowman+2016
   108	  join: Bowman's VizieR table carries no amplitudes; Mo+2026 supersedes it
   109	  (and is itself the published Murphy×Bowman merge, 1,838 stars).
   110	- Roster (`build_d3_roster.py`, rebuilt 2026-08-28 post-G1): gmag ≥ 13.2
   111	  (Murphy/KIC g magnitude — the named saturation proxy), ALL 610 dSct=1
   112	  survivors + ALL 76 dSct=2 (own class, excluded from headline numbers) +
   113	  2,314 dSct=0 negatives as a frozen-seed (20260828) simple random sample
   114	  (inclusion probability 0.317 recorded; sampling_weight column carried into
   115	  every weighted estimate) = 3,000. Amplitude coverage of positives:
   116	  456/610 with dominant amplitude; 48 > 10 mmag; 254 in 1–10; 154 < 1;
   117	  290 sub-hour; median 1.77 mmag. The 1–10 mmag log ladder and the
   118	  sub-threshold majority make the completeness turn-on curve the headline
   119	  D3 deliverable, not a defect (pre-registered: risk 2).
   120	- Acquisition: frozen `fetch_catalog_lightcurves.py --roster roster_d3.csv`
   121	  verbatim (10″ cone, 1.25 s cadence, resumable); frozen QC chain via
   122	  `build_panels_generic.py` (nearest-cluster crossmatch, catflags/chi cuts,
   123	  ≥20 exp/band, BJD_TDB at Palomar — all frozen functions).
   124	- Prespecified subsets: crowding (sep < 1.0″, ≤3 objects in cone),
   125	  near-saturation (g < 14 flagged; g > 14 safe subset).
   126	- Caveat on record: dSct=0 means "not a delta Scuti", not "constant" — the
   127	  D3 negative-class result is a TRIGGER RATE (never called FPR); triggered
   128	  negatives get adjudicated in W4 (plausible real variable vs unexplained).
   129	
   130	## D2 — TESS-truth transplant (DAV signals in real ZTF windows)
   131	
   132	- Truth: Romero+2022 (MNRAS 511, 1574; arXiv:2201.04158; 74 new DAVs,
   133	  TESS Cy1–3) + Romero+2025 (ApJ 984, 112; arXiv:2407.07260; 32 new DAVs,
   134	  Cy4–5). Published per-mode tables: period [s] + amplitude [ppt] + per-star
   135	  FAP(1/1000) limit + 20-s-cadence flags. 2025 revisions apply: NOV
   136	  retractions (TIC 261400271, 804835539, 317620456) and updated mode lists
   137	  for re-observed 2022 objects — latest published solution wins.
   138	- Truth model, not interpolation (`d2_truth_model.py`): DAV P < 240 s is
   139	  super-Nyquist AND past the first sinc null of TESS 120-s data; the mode
   140	  table is evaluated analytically at the template's real `bjd_tdb`.
   141	  Chain: ppt → mag (×1.0857e-3) → de-dilution OFF by default (SPOC PDCSAP is
   142	  crowding-corrected; ON = prespecified variant) → de-integrate TESS sinc
   143	  (reject modes with |sinc| < 0.3, i.e. P < ~160 s from 120-s data; prefer
   144	  20-s cadence solutions) → bandpass ladder A_g/A_TESS ∈ {1.4, 1.7, 2.1} ×
   145	  A_r/A_g ∈ {0.70, 0.80, 0.90} (nominal 1.7/0.80 from an in-code blackbody
   146	  derivative; the ladder is non-optional — zr carries most published
   147	  confirmations) → re-integrate ZTF 30-s sinc analytically → compose
   148	  phase-coherently in zg and zr (shared t_ref) so the frozen two-band rule
   149	  keeps its meaning.
   150	- Windows: templates from ALL 928 stars of the published catalog (G1 fix —
   151	  the earlier 510-not-detected pool conditioned on the pipeline's own
   152	  outcome), matched by median zg mag (|Δg| ≤ 0.25, widened when thin;
   153	  flagged), K=3 per target at 10/50/90th percentile of exposures-per-night
   154	  (75% of zg nights are single-exposure; per-night median subtraction
   155	  annihilates 53% of zg data — pre-registered, stratified: risk 3).
   156	  Native variability in the pool is handled by strict frequency-matched
   157	  scoring plus PAIRED UNINJECTED CONTROLS (95-prefix): one control shard per
   158	  unique arm-B template window. W2 stretch: fetch real ZTF light curves at
   159	  the 103 Romero positions; where the frozen QC crossmatch succeeds, those
   160	  self-windows become the preferred templates (removes template-choice
   161	  conditioning entirely for that subset).
   162	- Arms: B primary (signal + real ZTF mags, real magerr), A diagnostic
   163	  (synthetic Gaussian floor). FPR: 1,000 arm-A zero-amplitude nulls
   164	  (510 not-detected windows, fresh deterministic noise seeds where windows
   165	  repeat — windows repeat, noise does not; documented). Arm-B nulls are
   166	  tautological (templates ARE the not-detected set).
   167	  Verification arm: ~20 SPOC light curves prewhitened to confirm published
   168	  solutions; everything else needs metadata only.
   169	- Run matrix (sized to the 1-day wall budget at 22 workers ≈ 84 stars/h):
   170	  arm B nominal (1.7/0.80) 103×3 templates = 309; arm A nominal 309;
   171	  nulls 1,000; ladder sensitivity = 8 remaining (R_g, R_rg) points × 103 ×
   172	  1 template (the median-n_exp one) = 824. Total ≈ 2,442 ≈ 1.2 d.
   173	  De-dilution variant runs only for the SPOC verification-arm stars (dilution
   174	  factors are not in the papers; CROWDSAP comes with the ~20 downloads).
   175	  Post-G1 additions: paired controls (~<=309, prefix 95) and a phase-draw
   176	  sensitivity axis (2 extra deterministic phase draws x 103 targets on the
   177	  median template, arm B nominal) ≈ +515 runs; total ≈ 2,960 ≈ 1.5 d.
   178	- Truth-model corrections found at implementation (2026-08-28): |sinc| ≥ 0.3
   179	  rejection corresponds to P < ~160 s at 120-s cadence (the earlier "197 s"
   180	  was the |sinc| = 0.5 point); D2 min published period is 115.9 s and 49/103
   181	  stars carry 20-s solutions, so few modes are affected. Phases are
   182	  unpublished: drawn once per star from PCG64(seed=TIC), shared across bands
   183	  and ladder variants. Blackbody derivative at 11,500 K gives (1.43, 0.80) —
   184	  the ladder's low rung; upper rungs cover atmosphere-model/limb-darkening
   185	  uncertainty.
   186	
   187	## Metrics — see METRICS_SPEC.md (frozen before any campaign L-S run)
   188	
   189	## Execution topology
   190	
   191	- Mac: rosters, fetches, shard building, metrics, figures, git (authoritative).
   192	- Laptop `jacks-7i-5090` (22 workers): replay gate + D3 run. Desktop
   193	  (needs wake; offline 64 d): D2 + D3 overflow; if unreachable, D2 runs on
   194	  the laptop after D3 (+1 day; slip rule below).
   195	- Windows job launches escape the sshd job object via WMI
   196	  `Win32_Process.Create` (Start-Process children die with the ssh session —
   197	  found the hard way on the first replay launch).
   198	- Wall model (anchor 928 ≈ 11 h at 22 workers; cost scales with baseline):
   199	  D3@3,000 ≈ 1.2–1.9 d; D2 ≈ 1 d; hard stop via 150-star timing pilot.
   200	  Disk binds, not time: `workers = min(22, floor(free_GB × 0.5 / 0.47))`,
   201	  scratch on local NVMe/RAM disk, never a synced folder.
   202	- Results bundles: `generalization/results/<date>_<dataset>/` mirroring the
   203	  existing convention (README, DATA_PROVENANCE, SHA256SUMS, acceptance.json).
   204	
   205	## Review gates (sol@xhigh + ChatGPT Pro standing directive)
   206	
   207	| Gate | When | Reviewer | Scope |
   208	|---|---|---|---|
   209	| G1 | DONE 2026-08-28 | sol ×3 | 47 findings; dispositions in reviews/G1/RESPONSE.md; design fixes applied same day |
   210	| G2 | end W1 | sol ×5 | this file + METRICS_SPEC.md; frozen only after unanimous/addressed |
   211	| G3 | W2 pre-batch | Pro (inline code) | d2_truth_model + build_d2_shards: sinc algebra, bandpass, phase coherence, schema |
   212	| G4 | W3 mid-run | sol ×2 | pilot metrics sanity, run anomalies |
   213	| G5 | W4 | Pro + fresh-context verifier | results audit; every headline number re-derived from JSONs/CSVs |
   214	| G6 | Sep 26–29 | sol ×3 + ars-abstract | final abstract |
   215	
   216	## Timeline
   217	
   218	- W1 (Aug 28–Sep 3): tag+branch ✓, replay gate ✓(running), env pinning ✓,
   219	  frozen_api+tests ✓, D3 roster ✓, D3 IRSA fetch (overnight, running),
   220	  D2 sources downloaded ✓, PLAN+SPEC (this commit), G1, G2, D2 roster parser.
   221	- W2 (Sep 4–10): build_panels_generic on D3 → census; d2_truth_model + tests
   222	  + G3; build_d2_shards; verify_cli_identity; 150-star pilot; wake desktop.
   223	- W3 (Sep 11–17): D3 full run (laptop) ∥ D2 (desktop); metrics+plots against
   224	  pilot output; G4.
   225	- W4 (Sep 18–25): metrics, ladders, figures, bundles, acceptance; G5;
   226	  cross-dataset synthesis table.
   227	- Sep 26–30: abstract + G6; submit.
   228	- Slip rule (revised at G1 — the old "D2 alone flips the condition" claim is
   229	  untenable since D2 is not an externally labeled sample): D3 is the dataset
   230	  that satisfies the external-label condition; if only ONE new dataset can
   231	  land by Sep 25 it must be D3, with D2 stated as in progress. If only D2
   232	  lands, the abstract is scoped to injection-recovery + D1 and makes no
   233	  external-validation claim.
   234	
   235	## Top risks
   236	
   237	1. Env fails replay → pin/iterate until byte-identical; blocks all work.
   238	2. D3 completeness ≈ 0 below the a95 floor → stratification IS the
   239	   deliverable (turn-on curve).
   240	3. D2 high-pass ≈ 0 from the single-exposure-night penalty → pre-registered
   241	   expected headline, stratified to be explanatory.
   242	4. A_r/A_g lever → mandatory ladder; headline reported as a band.
   243	5. D3 negatives not constants → FPR an upper bound, stated.
   244	6. Desktop unreachable → D2 on laptop after D3 (+1 day).
   245	7. Romero mode tables are LaTeX prose with typos (comma decimals, stray
   246	   units) → parser with hard row-count and range asserts; G3 reviews the
   247	   parsed output against the PDFs.
   248	
   249	## Mandatory citations
   250	
   251	Sokolovsky+2017 (variability-index benchmark; data not public — comparison
   252	baseline only), Guidry+2021, Hermes+2017, Murphy+2019, Bowman+2016 (context),
   253	Mo+2026, Romero+2022, Romero+2025, Gentile Fusillo+2021, Masci+2019.
     1	# METRICS_SPEC — frozen before any campaign Lomb-Scargle run
     2	
     3	Implemented by `scripts/generalization/metrics_generalization.py`. Any change
     4	after the first campaign L-S run voids the prespecification and must be
     5	reported as such. Revised at G1 (2026-08-28) in response to the sol review
     6	panel — see `generalization/reviews/G1/RESPONSE.md`; frozen at G2.
     7	
     8	## Estimand vocabulary (names are binding)
     9	
    10	The campaign does NOT produce a single pooled "selection function". It
    11	produces three separate response assessments with these named estimands:
    12	
    13	- **detection completeness** — P(rule fires | labeled positive), per dataset,
    14	  class, pass rule. D3 denominator: all 610 dSct=1 (external labels).
    15	  D2 denominator: injection targets (synthetic positives — reported as
    16	  *conditional injection-recovery efficiency of the search stage*, never as
    17	  real-sky completeness).
    18	- **frequency-recovery completeness** — P(rule fires AND strict frequency
    19	  match | labeled positive AND frequency-scorable). D3 frequency-scorable:
    20	  the 456/610 with Mo+2026 rows (reported as "Mo-join-conditioned"; joined
    21	  vs unjoined covariates compared). D2: targets with >=1 injected mode
    22	  inside the pass's search bounds after sinc rejection (S_p = 1).
    23	  The missed-vs-wrong-frequency decomposition uses ONLY matching
    24	  denominators (both conditional on scorable/S_p = 1).
    25	- **correct-frequency fraction among detected positives** — what an earlier
    26	  draft called "purity"; it is not positive predictive value and is never
    27	  labeled purity. Class-level PPV is reported for D3 only, with sampling
    28	  weights (negatives carry weight pool/sample = 7292/2314), as a
    29	  prevalence-weighted estimate with the contaminated-negative caveat.
    30	- **negative-class trigger rate** — P(rule fires | Murphy dSct=0). NOT called
    31	  FPR: the class contains non-dSct variables; reported with sampling weights
    32	  and, after adjudication of triggered negatives (W4), split into
    33	  "plausible real variable" vs "unexplained".
    34	- **Gaussian-null false-alarm rate (FPR_Gaussian)** — P(confirmed | arm-A
    35	  zero-amplitude null), n = 1000 over the 928-window frame (windows repeat,
    36	  seeds do not). Acceptance criterion (preregistered): one-sided 95% upper
    37	  bound <= 0.5% at zero events. The FP frequency-distribution/alias audit is
    38	  descriptive only below 10 events.
    39	- **native trigger rate of the template pool** — P(confirmed | paired
    40	  uninjected control window), the 95-prefix arm. Context for D2 recovery,
    41	  not an FPR.
    42	
    43	## Frequency-match taxonomy (disjoint labels, strict first)
    44	
    45	Tolerance: 1.5 / baseline_days per star (the pipeline's own convention) plus
    46	a dataset truth-quantum term for truth-table rounding: D1 +0.0025 / d
    47	(literature frequencies tabulated to 2 decimals), D2/D3 +0 (exact / 6-decimal
    48	uHz). D1 truth frequencies are additionally NON-CONTEMPORANEOUS single-epoch
    49	tabulations of multi-mode pulsators (observed lit-vs-ZTF offsets reach 0.6%),
    50	so D1 frequency-recovery is reported as a DIAGNOSTIC only; D1's estimand is
    51	detection completeness. D1 labels come from the published master table
    52	(19 usable stars; 13 paper-variable, 5 paper-constant) with the frozen
    53	pipeline's eclipsing sanity control (2833849800205759360) excluded as class
    54	`transit_control` — it is a known variable and can serve neither class.
    55	Validation on record (2026-08-28): metrics_generalization on the published
    56	bundle reproduces all five published D1 numbers (11/13 L-S, 9/13 census,
    57	13/13 union, 0 confirmed + 1 candidate among 5 constants).
    58	For each detected candidate, in precedence order against the truth list
    59	(D3: Mo frequencies for that KIC; D2: injected modes):
    60	
    61	1. `direct` — within tolerance of a truth frequency;
    62	2. `harmonic` — within tolerance of 2f or f/2 of a truth frequency;
    63	3. `window_alias` — within tolerance of |f_truth ± k f_sid|, k = 1, 2
    64	   (sidereal-day family, the pipeline's own alias model);
    65	4. `ambiguous` — matches >1 truth frequency class above;
    66	5. `unmatched`.
    67	
    68	Headline frequency recovery counts `direct` only, scored against the
    69	pipeline's BEST candidate (`matched_primary`). D3's primary truth frequency
    70	is the DOMINANT Mo mode; any-mode direct matches are a secondary column.
    71	`matched_any_mode` over the 15 stored top_peaks is diagnostic only.
    72	Chance-match calibration: truth lists permuted across stars (frozen seed,
    73	100 permutations) → accidental direct-match rate reported beside every
    74	frequency-recovery table.
    75	
    76	## Detection rules (all four always reported; PRIMARY = rule 1)
    77	
    78	1. `confirmed` (headline), 2. `confirmed|candidate`, 3. `census`
    79	(any of six frozen ratios >= 2.5), 4. `either` (1 OR 3).
    80	Primary claim family (preregistered): rule 1, pass = best of {low, high}
    81	(the frozen `overall_result` ordering), nominal D2 variant (1.7/0.80,
    82	de-dilution off, arm B), per dataset. Everything else is labeled a
    83	pointwise descriptive sensitivity analysis; no simultaneous-coverage claim.
    84	
    85	## Units of analysis and intervals
    86	
    87	- D1/D3: the star is the unit; Wilson 95% intervals on independent per-star
    88	  proportions; weighted estimates use the effective-sample-size Wilson
    89	  approximation.
    90	- D2: the TESS target is the CLUSTER. K=3 template windows and ladder/phase
    91	  variants are correlated replicates, never pooled as independent trials.
    92	  Per-stratum (10/50/90th percentile window) proportions are reported
    93	  separately; aggregates are equal-weight standardized means over targets
    94	  with cluster bootstrap intervals (resample targets, keep all replicates;
    95	  B = 2000, frozen seed). Ladder results: nominal is primary; the min-max
    96	  across the 3x3 grid is a "prespecified finite-grid sensitivity range",
    97	  never a confidence band; endpoint scenarios identified.
    98	
    99	## Complementarity (census vs L-S)
   100	
   101	Primary table (per dataset, on labeled positives with both methods
   102	available): C = census flag; L = rule-1 detection (detection-only, no
   103	frequency requirement — symmetric margins). Report the full 2x2, both
   104	discordant fractions, union completeness, and incremental yields
   105	P(C=1,L=0), P(C=0,L=1) with intervals (Wilson for D3/D1; cluster bootstrap
   106	for D2). Exact McNemar is SECONDARY (marginal-homogeneity only; it does not
   107	measure complementarity).
   108	
   109	## Surfaces
   110	
   111	Completeness on (log P, log A) and (median exposures-per-night, log A).
   112	Amplitude axis is INVARIANT per dataset: D3 = historical Kepler-band
   113	dominant amplitude (mmag; explicitly non-contemporaneous, not a ZTF-g
   114	threshold); D2 = published TESS amplitude (ppt) for cross-variant surfaces,
   115	nominal injected A_g for the nominal-only surface. Bin edges frozen here:
   116	log P edges at P = {100 s, 200 s, 500 s, 1000 s, 2000 s, 0.05 d, 0.2 d,
   117	1 d, 10 d, 100 d}; amplitude edges {0.5, 1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 50, 200} mmag
   118	(D3) / {0.5, 2, 5, 10, 30, 100} ppt (D2); cells below 5 stars reported as
   119	counts only, no proportion.
   120	
   121	## Eligibility and attrition
   122	
   123	Two denominators, both always reported: P(rule | eligible roster target) and
   124	P(rule | usable light curve) (frozen QC crossmatch passed, both passes
   125	available). A full attrition table (roster -> fetched -> crossmatched ->
   126	QC-passed -> both-passes-complete) by class, amplitude stratum, and
   127	magnitude accompanies every dataset. Unavailable passes are never silently
   128	dropped.
   129	
   130	## Guards
   131	
   132	- Assert no campaign census ratio equals 2.5 exactly.
   133	- Assert every scored JSON has complete == true; both passes present.
   134	- Manifest: SHA-256 of every input file, env versions, frozen + campaign
   135	  file SHAs (frozen_api.campaign_file_shas), replay attestation reference,
   136	  spec git blob SHA.
   137	
   138	## Outputs
   139	
   140	`generalization/results/<date>_<dataset>/metrics/`: per_star.csv,
   141	completeness_by_class_pass_rule.csv, contingency_complementarity.json,
   142	trigger_rates.csv, fp_frequency_distribution.csv, chance_match.csv,
   143	surfaces/*.csv, sensitivity.csv, attrition.csv, manifest.json.
   144	Figures via plot_generalization.py from these CSVs only.
     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""D2 truth model: analytic DAV signals for injection into real ZTF windows.
     3	
     4	Why a truth model and not interpolation: DAV periods reach below twice the
     5	TESS 120-s cadence (super-Nyquist) and below the first sinc null; interpolated
     6	TESS photometry is undefined there. The published mode solution (period,
     7	amplitude) IS the measurement — we evaluate it analytically at the template's
     8	real BJD_TDB epochs.
     9	
    10	Amplitude chain (GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md, D2):
    11	  A_ppt (published, TESS-integrated)
    12	    -> fractional flux (x 1e-3)
    13	    -> de-dilution OFF by default (SPOC PDCSAP is crowding-corrected;
    14	       ON = prespecified variant, divides by the published dilution if given)
    15	    -> de-integrate the TESS exposure: divide by sinc(pi f T_cad);
    16	       REJECT modes with |sinc| < 0.3 (do not amplify model error > 3.3x).
    17	       Note: at T=120 s this cutoff is P < ~160.1 s (the plan text said
    18	       "197 s", which is the |sinc| = 0.5 point — arithmetic slip, criterion
    19	       |sinc| >= 0.3 is what was prespecified and is what runs).
    20	    -> magnitudes (x 1.0857)
    21	    -> bandpass ladder: A_g = R_g * A_TESS_intrinsic, A_r = R_rg * A_g with
    22	       R_g in {1.4, 1.7, 2.1}, R_rg in {0.70, 0.80, 0.90}; blackbody T-derivative
    23	       ratios at Teff ~ 11,500 K give (1.43, 0.80) — the ladder's low rung;
    24	       empirical DAV multi-band ratios (limb darkening + nonadiabatic boost in
    25	       the blue) motivate the upper rungs. Nominal (1.7, 0.80). Headline
    26	       numbers are quoted as the band across the ladder.
    27	    -> re-integrate the ZTF 30-s exposure: multiply by sinc(pi f 30s).
    28	
    29	Phases are unpublished: drawn once per star from PCG64(seed=TIC), shared
    30	across bands and across every ladder variant (variant-stable), with a shared
    31	t_ref so the two-band evidence rule keeps its meaning.
    32	"""
    33	
    34	from __future__ import annotations
    35	
    36	import math
    37	from dataclasses import dataclass, field
    38	
    39	import numpy as np
    40	
    41	PPT_TO_FRAC = 1.0e-3
    42	FRAC_TO_MAG = 1.0857
    43	ZTF_EXPOSURE_S = 30.0
    44	SINC_REJECT_BELOW = 0.3
    45	BANDPASS_LADDER_G = (1.4, 1.7, 2.1)
    46	BANDPASS_LADDER_RG = (0.70, 0.80, 0.90)
    47	NOMINAL_G = 1.7
    48	NOMINAL_RG = 0.80
    49	
    50	# band-effective wavelengths [nm] for the blackbody-derivative check
    51	LAMBDA_NM = {"zg": 472.0, "zr": 642.0, "tess": 786.0}
    52	HC_OVER_K_NM_K = 1.43877688e7  # h c / k_B in nm*K
    53	
    54	
    55	def integration_sinc(period_s: float, t_int_s: float) -> float:
    56	    """Signed attenuation of a sinusoid amplitude under boxcar integration."""
    57	    x = math.pi * t_int_s / period_s
    58	    return 1.0 if x == 0.0 else math.sin(x) / x
    59	
    60	
    61	def blackbody_dlnB_dlnT(wavelength_nm: float, teff_k: float) -> float:
    62	    x = HC_OVER_K_NM_K / (wavelength_nm * teff_k)
    63	    return x / (1.0 - math.exp(-x))
    64	
    65	
    66	def blackbody_amplitude_ratios(teff_k: float = 11500.0) -> tuple[float, float]:
    67	    """(A_g/A_TESS, A_r/A_g) for pure temperature perturbations."""
    68	    g = blackbody_dlnB_dlnT(LAMBDA_NM["zg"], teff_k)
    69	    r = blackbody_dlnB_dlnT(LAMBDA_NM["zr"], teff_k)
    70	    tess = blackbody_dlnB_dlnT(LAMBDA_NM["tess"], teff_k)
    71	    return g / tess, r / g
    72	
    73	
    74	@dataclass(frozen=True)
    75	class TruthMode:
    76	    period_s: float
    77	    frequency_per_day: float
    78	    amp_tess_ppt: float
    79	    tess_sinc: float
    80	    amp_g_mag: float          # intrinsic zg amplitude after ladder, before ZTF sinc
    81	    amp_r_mag: float
    82	    ztf_sinc: float
    83	    phase_rad: float
    84	
    85	
    86	@dataclass(frozen=True)
    87	class TruthModel:
    88	    tic: int
    89	    cadence_s: float
    90	    ratio_g: float
    91	    ratio_rg: float
    92	    dedilution: float | None
    93	    modes: tuple[TruthMode, ...]
    94	    rejected: tuple[dict, ...] = field(default=())
    95	
    96	    def evaluate(self, bjd_tdb: np.ndarray, band: str, t_ref: float) -> np.ndarray:
    97	        """Delta-mag time series at the template's real epochs (days)."""
    98	        if band not in ("zg", "zr"):
    99	            raise ValueError(band)
   100	        delta = np.zeros_like(np.asarray(bjd_tdb, dtype=float))
   101	        for mode in self.modes:
   102	            amp = mode.amp_g_mag if band == "zg" else mode.amp_r_mag
   103	            amp *= mode.ztf_sinc
   104	            phase = 2.0 * np.pi * mode.frequency_per_day * (bjd_tdb - t_ref)
   105	            delta += amp * np.cos(phase + mode.phase_rad)
   106	        return delta
   107	
   108	
   109	def build_truth_model(
   110	    tic: int,
   111	    periods_s: list[float],
   112	    amps_ppt: list[float],
   113	    cadence_s: float,
   114	    ratio_g: float = NOMINAL_G,
   115	    ratio_rg: float = NOMINAL_RG,
   116	    dedilution: float | None = None,
   117	    amplitude_scale: float = 1.0,
   118	) -> TruthModel:
   119	    """amplitude_scale=0.0 builds a zero-amplitude null with the same modes."""
   120	    if len(periods_s) != len(amps_ppt):
   121	        raise ValueError("periods and amplitudes must align")
   122	    rng = np.random.Generator(np.random.PCG64(int(tic)))
   123	    phases = rng.uniform(0.0, 2.0 * np.pi, size=len(periods_s))
   124	    modes: list[TruthMode] = []
   125	    rejected: list[dict] = []
   126	    for period, amp_ppt, phase in zip(periods_s, amps_ppt, phases):
   127	        tess_sinc = integration_sinc(period, cadence_s)
   128	        if abs(tess_sinc) < SINC_REJECT_BELOW:
   129	            rejected.append(
   130	                {"period_s": period, "amp_ppt": amp_ppt, "tess_sinc": tess_sinc}
   131	            )
   132	            continue
   133	        frac = amp_ppt * PPT_TO_FRAC * amplitude_scale
   134	        if dedilution is not None:
   135	            frac /= dedilution
   136	        intrinsic_frac = frac / tess_sinc  # signed: negative sinc = pi phase flip
   137	        amp_tess_mag = intrinsic_frac * FRAC_TO_MAG
   138	        modes.append(
   139	            TruthMode(
   140	                period_s=period,
   141	                frequency_per_day=86400.0 / period,
   142	                amp_tess_ppt=amp_ppt,
   143	                tess_sinc=tess_sinc,
   144	                amp_g_mag=amp_tess_mag * ratio_g,
   145	                amp_r_mag=amp_tess_mag * ratio_g * ratio_rg,
   146	                ztf_sinc=integration_sinc(period, ZTF_EXPOSURE_S),
   147	                phase_rad=float(phase),
   148	            )
   149	        )
   150	    return TruthModel(
   151	        tic=tic,
   152	        cadence_s=cadence_s,
   153	        ratio_g=ratio_g,
   154	        ratio_rg=ratio_rg,
   155	        dedilution=dedilution,
   156	        modes=tuple(modes),
   157	        rejected=tuple(rejected),
   158	    )
     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""Build the D2 truth roster from the Romero TESS DAV papers.
     3	
     4	Parses the published per-mode tables (period [s], amplitude [ppt]) from the
     5	arXiv LaTeX sources cached in generalization/data/d2/raw:
     6	  Romero+2022  arXiv:2201.04158 (MNRAS 511, 1574)  74 new DAVs, Cycles 1-3
     7	  Romero+2025  arXiv:2407.07260 (ApJ 984, 112)     32 new DAVs, Cycles 4-5
     8	               + Table "old": revised mode lists for re-observed 2022 DAVs,
     9	               including NOV retractions.
    10	
    11	Supersede policy (prespecified): the latest published solution per TIC wins —
    12	2025 "old" table over 2022; NOV objects are dropped from the roster entirely.
    13	
    14	The LaTeX tables contain human typos (comma decimals `356,09`, stray unit
    15	`503.99s`, one missing close-paren, missing list commas). The parser
    16	normalizes these mechanically and then enforces hard range/count asserts;
    17	G3 reviews the parsed output against the paper PDFs.
    18	"""
    19	
    20	from __future__ import annotations
    21	
    22	import argparse
    23	import hashlib
    24	import json
    25	import re
    26	from pathlib import Path
    27	
    28	import pandas as pd
    29	
    30	from frozen_api import REPO_ROOT, assert_frozen
    31	
    32	RAW = REPO_ROOT / "generalization/data/d2/raw"
    33	NOV_TICS = {261400271, 804835539, 317620456}
    34	# TIC 683837451 is in the 2022 mode table but its Table-1 row is commented out
    35	# in the arXiv source (NewTess.tex line ~260: "%0683837451 & 045827.11 &
    36	# $-$654003.4 & 17.40 & ..."); values transcribed from that commented row.
    37	CURATED_META = {
    38	    683837451: {
    39	        "ra": 15.0 * (4.0 + 58.0 / 60.0 + 27.11 / 3600.0),
    40	        "dec": -(65.0 + 40.0 / 60.0 + 3.4 / 3600.0),
    41	        "gmag": 17.40,
    42	    }
    43	}
    44	MODE_PAIR = re.compile(r"(\d+\.\d+)\s*s?\s*\(\s*(\d+\.?\d*)\s*[)}]?")
    45	
    46	
    47	def strip_row(line: str) -> str:
    48	    # drop unescaped % comments, row terminator, italics markup, math mode
    49	    out = []
    50	    for index, char in enumerate(line):
    51	        if char == "%" and (index == 0 or line[index - 1] != "\\"):
    52	            break
    53	        out.append(char)
    54	    text = "".join(out)
    55	    text = text.replace("\\\\", "").replace("{\\it", " ").replace("\\textit{", " ")
    56	    text = text.replace("{", " ").replace("}", " ").replace("$", "")
    57	    return text.strip()
    58	
    59	
    60	def table_rows(source: str, header_pattern: str, count: int = 1) -> list[list[str]]:
    61	    """All `&`-separated rows from tables whose header matches header_pattern."""
    62	    rows: list[list[str]] = []
    63	    seen = 0
    64	    for block in re.split(r"\\begin\{table\*?\}", source)[1:]:
    65	        body = block.split("\\end{table")[0]
    66	        if not re.search(header_pattern, body):
    67	            continue
    68	        seen += 1
    69	        for line in body.splitlines():
    70	            if "&" not in line or "\\hline" in line:
    71	                continue
    72	            cleaned = strip_row(line)
    73	            if not cleaned or re.search(header_pattern, line):
    74	                continue
    75	            rows.append([cell.strip() for cell in cleaned.split("&")])
    76	    if seen < count:
    77	        raise SystemExit(f"found {seen} tables matching {header_pattern!r}, expected >= {count}")
    78	    return rows
    79	
    80	
    81	def merge_continuations(rows: list[list[str]]) -> dict[int, list[list[str]]]:
    82	    """Group rows by TIC; a leading-cdots row continues the previous TIC."""
    83	    grouped: dict[int, list[list[str]]] = {}
    84	    current: int | None = None
    85	    for row in rows:
    86	        first = row[0].replace("\\cdots", "").strip()
    87	        if first.isdigit():
    88	            current = int(first)
    89	            grouped.setdefault(current, []).append(row)
    90	        elif current is not None:
    91	            grouped[current].append(row)
    92	    return grouped
    93	
    94	
    95	def parse_modes(cells: list[str]) -> list[tuple[float, float]]:
    96	    text = " , ".join(cells)
    97	    text = re.sub(r"(\d),(\d)", r"\1.\2", text)  # comma decimals -> dots
    98	    return [(float(p), float(a)) for p, a in MODE_PAIR.findall(text)]
    99	
   100	
   101	def parse_mode_table(source: str, paper: str) -> tuple[pd.DataFrame, pd.DataFrame]:
   102	    rows = table_rows(source, r"FAP\(1/1000\)\s*\[ppt\]")
   103	    modes: list[dict] = []
   104	    stars: list[dict] = []
   105	    for tic, group in merge_continuations(rows).items():
   106	        sectors = group[0][1]
   107	        fap_text = group[0][2].strip()
   108	        mode_cells = [row[3] for row in group if len(row) > 3]
   109	        extra_sectors = [
   110	            row[1] for row in group[1:]
   111	            if len(row) > 1 and re.search(r"\d", row[1].replace("\\cdots", ""))
   112	        ]
   113	        if extra_sectors:
   114	            sectors = sectors.rstrip(", ") + "," + ",".join(extra_sectors)
   115	        is_nov = any("NOV" in cell for cell in mode_cells)
   116	        pairs = [] if is_nov else parse_modes(mode_cells)
   117	        if not is_nov and not pairs:
   118	            raise SystemExit(f"{paper} TIC {tic}: no modes parsed from {mode_cells!r}")
   119	        stars.append(
   120	            {
   121	                "tic": tic,
   122	                "paper": paper,
   123	                "sectors": re.sub(r"\s+", "", sectors),
   124	                "fap_ppt": float(fap_text),
   125	                "cadence_s": 20 if "f" in sectors else 120,
   126	                "nov": is_nov,
   127	                "n_modes": len(pairs),
   128	            }
   129	        )
   130	        for period, amp in pairs:
   131	            modes.append({"tic": tic, "paper": paper, "period_s": period, "amp_ppt": amp})
   132	    return pd.DataFrame(stars), pd.DataFrame(modes)
   133	
   134	
   135	def sexagesimal_to_deg(ra_text: str, dec_text: str) -> tuple[float, float]:
   136	    ra_text = ra_text.replace("\\", "").strip()
   137	    dec_text = dec_text.replace("\\", "").replace("−", "-").strip()
   138	    def split3(text: str) -> list[float]:
   139	        parts = text.split(":")
   140	        if len(parts) == 4:  # paper typo: colon used as the decimal point
   141	            parts = parts[:2] + [parts[2] + "." + parts[3]]
   142	        return [float(x) for x in parts]
   143	
   144	    if ":" in ra_text:
   145	        h, m, s = split3(ra_text)
   146	        dd, dm, ds = split3(dec_text.replace("+", ""))
   147	        sign = -1.0 if dec_text.lstrip().startswith("-") else 1.0
   148	    else:
   149	        h, m, s = float(ra_text[0:2]), float(ra_text[2:4]), float(ra_text[4:])
   150	        stripped = dec_text.lstrip("+-")
   151	        dd, dm, ds = float(stripped[0:2]), float(stripped[2:4]), float(stripped[4:])
   152	        sign = -1.0 if dec_text.startswith("-") else 1.0
   153	    return 15.0 * (h + m / 60.0 + s / 3600.0), sign * (abs(dd) + dm / 60.0 + ds / 3600.0)
   154	
   155	
   156	def parse_star_table(source: str, paper: str) -> pd.DataFrame:
   157	    rows = table_rows(source, r"RA\s*&\s*DEC")
   158	    records = []
   159	    for tic, group in merge_continuations(rows).items():
   160	        row = group[0]
   161	        ra, dec = sexagesimal_to_deg(row[1], row[2])
   162	        records.append(
   163	            {"tic": tic, "paper": paper, "ra": ra, "dec": dec, "gmag": float(row[3])}
   164	        )
   165	    return pd.DataFrame(records)
   166	
   167	
   168	def main() -> None:
   169	    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)
   170	    parser.add_argument("--out-dir", type=Path, default=REPO_ROOT / "generalization/data/d2")
   171	    args = parser.parse_args()
   172	    assert_frozen()
   173	
   174	    provenance = {
   175	        name: hashlib.sha256((RAW / name).read_bytes()).hexdigest()
   176	        for name in ("romero2022_src.tar.gz", "romero2025_src.tar.gz")
   177	    }
   178	    src2022 = (RAW / "romero2022_src/NewTess.tex").read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
   179	    src2025 = (RAW / "romero2025_src/NewTESS.tex").read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
   180	
   181	    # the 2025 file holds two mode tables: "new" (32) then "old" (revised
   182	    # R22); slice at the old table's begin marker (its caption sits inside
   183	    # the block, so slicing at the caption text would orphan the rows)
   184	    old_caption = src2025.find("showing a change in the period list")
   185	    if old_caption < 0:
   186	        raise SystemExit("2025 old-table caption not found")
   187	    old_start = src2025.rfind("\\begin{table", 0, old_caption)
   188	    stars22, modes22 = parse_mode_table(src2022, "romero2022")
   189	    stars25, modes25 = parse_mode_table(src2025[:old_start], "romero2025")
   190	    stars25old, modes25old = parse_mode_table(src2025[old_start:], "romero2025old")
   191	
   192	    if len(stars22) != 74:
   193	        raise SystemExit(f"2022 mode table: {len(stars22)} stars, expected 74")
   194	    if len(stars25) != 32:
   195	        raise SystemExit(f"2025 new mode table: {len(stars25)} stars, expected 32")
   196	    nov_found = set(stars25old.loc[stars25old["nov"], "tic"])
   197	    if nov_found != NOV_TICS:
   198	        raise SystemExit(f"NOV set {nov_found} != expected {NOV_TICS}")
   199	
   200	    meta22 = parse_star_table(src2022, "romero2022")
   201	    meta25 = parse_star_table(src2025, "romero2025")
   202	    meta = pd.concat([meta25, meta22], ignore_index=True).drop_duplicates("tic", keep="first")
   203	
   204	    # supersede: 2025old > 2022; drop NOV
   205	    solutions = {}
   206	    for frame in (stars22, stars25, stars25old):
   207	        for record in frame.to_dict("records"):
   208	            if record["paper"] == "romero2025old" or record["tic"] not in solutions:
   209	                solutions[record["tic"]] = record
   210	    targets = pd.DataFrame(
   211	        record for record in solutions.values() if not record["nov"]
   212	    ).sort_values("tic")
   213	    modes = pd.concat([modes22, modes25, modes25old], ignore_index=True)
   214	    chosen = modes.merge(
   215	        targets[["tic", "paper"]], on=["tic", "paper"], how="inner"
   216	    ).sort_values(["tic", "period_s"])
   217	
   218	    if not ((chosen["period_s"] >= 70.0) & (chosen["period_s"] <= 2200.0)).all():
   219	        bad = chosen[(chosen["period_s"] < 70.0) | (chosen["period_s"] > 2200.0)]
   220	        raise SystemExit(f"periods out of DAV range:\n{bad}")
   221	    if not ((chosen["amp_ppt"] > 0.0) & (chosen["amp_ppt"] <= 400.0)).all():
   222	        raise SystemExit("amplitudes out of range")
   223	    missing_meta = set(targets["tic"]) - set(meta["tic"])
   224	    curated = [
   225	        {"tic": tic, "paper": "curated", **CURATED_META[tic]}
   226	        for tic in missing_meta
   227	        if tic in CURATED_META
   228	    ]
   229	    if curated:
   230	        meta = pd.concat([meta, pd.DataFrame(curated)], ignore_index=True)
   231	        missing_meta -= set(CURATED_META)
   232	    if missing_meta:
   233	        raise SystemExit(f"targets missing star metadata: {sorted(missing_meta)[:5]}")
   234	
   235	    targets = targets.merge(meta[["tic", "ra", "dec", "gmag"]], on="tic", how="left")
   236	    args.out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
   237	    targets.to_csv(args.out_dir / "d2_targets.csv", index=False)
   238	    chosen.to_csv(args.out_dir / "d2_modes.csv", index=False)
   239	    modes.to_csv(args.out_dir / "d2_modes_all_solutions.csv", index=False)
   240	
   241	    report = {
   242	        "targets": len(targets),
   243	        "from_2022_only": int((targets["paper"] == "romero2022").sum()),
   244	        "from_2025_new": int((targets["paper"] == "romero2025").sum()),
   245	        "superseded_by_2025old": int((targets["paper"] == "romero2025old").sum()),
   246	        "nov_dropped": sorted(NOV_TICS),
   247	        "modes_total": len(chosen),
   248	        "modes_per_star_median": float(targets["n_modes"].median()),
   249	        "period_s_range": [float(chosen["period_s"].min()), float(chosen["period_s"].max())],
   250	        "amp_ppt_range": [float(chosen["amp_ppt"].min()), float(chosen["amp_ppt"].max())],
   251	        "stars_with_20s_cadence": int((targets["cadence_s"] == 20).sum()),
   252	        "gmag_range": [float(targets["gmag"].min()), float(targets["gmag"].max())],
   253	        "provenance_sha256": provenance,
   254	    }
   255	    (args.out_dir / "d2_roster_report.json").write_text(
   256	        json.dumps(report, indent=2) + "\n", encoding="utf-8"
   257	    )
   258	    print(json.dumps(report, indent=2))
   259	
   260	
   261	if __name__ == "__main__":
   262	    main()
     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""Build the D3 roster: ZTF x Kepler delta Scuti with external truth labels.
     3	
     4	Sources (VizieR, cached under generalization/data/d3/raw with SHA-256 recorded):
     5	  Murphy+2019  J/MNRAS/485/2380/table1  14,330 Kepler A/F stars; dSct flag
     6	               0 = not delta Sct (labeled negative class), 1 = delta Sct,
     7	               2 = ambiguous (kept as its own class, excluded from headline
     8	               completeness/FPR); gmag; positions.
     9	  Mo+2026      J/A+A/710/A245/table2    259,883 extracted frequencies (SNR>8)
    10	               for 1,838 Kepler delta Sct stars; per-star dominant amplitude
    11	               (ppt) and its frequency (uHz).
    12	  Mo+2026      J/A+A/710/A245/table1    15,265 confirmed super-Nyquist
    13	               frequencies in 1,309 stars; any confirmed SNF implies a real
    14	               mode above the Kepler LC Nyquist (283.2 uHz), i.e. P < 59 min
    15	               -> the sub-hour stratum.
    16	
    17	Selection:
    18	  gmag >= 13.2 (ZTF saturation; gmag is the Murphy/KIC g magnitude); ALL
    19	  dSct=1 (610) and dSct=2 (76) survivors; dSct=0 negatives drawn as a
    20	  frozen-seed simple random sample (seed 20260828) with the inclusion
    21	  probability recorded and a sampling_weight column carried into metrics.
    22	
    23	Labels are obtained independently of the frozen ZTF pipeline. Negatives are
    24	"not a delta Sct", not "constant": the D3 negative-class result is a TRIGGER
    25	RATE, never an FPR (GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md risk 5; estimand names in
    26	METRICS_SPEC.md are binding).
    27	"""
    28	
    29	from __future__ import annotations
    30	
    31	import argparse
    32	import hashlib
    33	import io
    34	import json
    35	import time
    36	import urllib.parse
    37	import urllib.request
    38	from pathlib import Path
    39	
    40	import numpy as np
    41	import pandas as pd
    42	
    43	from frozen_api import REPO_ROOT, assert_frozen, campaign_id_ok
    44	
    45	TAP_SYNC = "https://tapvizier.cds.unistra.fr/TAPVizieR/tap/sync"
    46	PPT_TO_MMAG = 1.0857  # dm = -2.5 log10(1 + dF/F) ~= 1.0857 (dF/F); 1 ppt -> 1.0857 mmag
    47	UHZ_TO_PER_DAY = 86400.0 / 1e6
    48	KEPLER_LC_NYQUIST_UHZ = 283.2
    49	NEGATIVE_SAMPLE_SEED = 20260828
    50	
    51	QUERIES = {
    52	    "murphy2019_table1.csv": 'SELECT KIC, GaiaDR2, gmag, Teff, logg, dSct, _RA, _DE '
    53	                             'FROM "J/MNRAS/485/2380/table1"',
    54	    "mo2026_table2.csv": 'SELECT KIC, Freq, Amp FROM "J/A+A/710/A245/table2"',
    55	    "mo2026_table1.csv": 'SELECT KIC, Freq, Amp, fR, C, SC FROM "J/A+A/710/A245/table1"',
    56	}
    57	
    58	
    59	def tap_fetch(query: str, retries: int = 4) -> str:
    60	    payload = urllib.parse.urlencode(
    61	        {"REQUEST": "doQuery", "LANG": "ADQL", "FORMAT": "csv", "QUERY": query}
    62	    ).encode()
    63	    for attempt in range(retries + 1):
    64	        try:
    65	            request = urllib.request.Request(TAP_SYNC, data=payload)
    66	            with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=300) as response:
    67	                text = response.read().decode("utf-8")
    68	            if text.lstrip().startswith("<?xml"):
    69	                raise RuntimeError(f"TAP error response: {text[:300]}")
    70	            return text
    71	        except Exception:
    72	            if attempt == retries:
    73	                raise
    74	            time.sleep(5.0 * (attempt + 1))
    75	    raise RuntimeError("unreachable")
    76	
    77	
    78	def cached_pull(raw_dir: Path, name: str, provenance: dict) -> pd.DataFrame:
    79	    path = raw_dir / name
    80	    if not path.exists():
    81	        text = tap_fetch(QUERIES[name])
    82	        path.write_text(text, encoding="utf-8", newline="")
    83	    raw = path.read_bytes()
    84	    provenance[name] = {
    85	        "query": QUERIES[name],
    86	        "sha256": hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest(),
    87	        "bytes": len(raw),
    88	    }
    89	    return pd.read_csv(io.BytesIO(raw))
    90	
    91	
    92	def campaign_id_for_kic(kic: int) -> str:
    93	    return "90" + str(int(kic)).zfill(17)
    94	
    95	
    96	def amp_ladder_stratum(amp_mmag: float, subhour: bool) -> str:
    97	    if subhour:
    98	        return "subhour"
    99	    if not np.isfinite(amp_mmag):
   100	        return "amp_unknown"
   101	    if amp_mmag > 10.0:
   102	        return "amp_gt10"
   103	    if amp_mmag >= 1.0:
   104	        edges = np.logspace(0.0, 1.0, 7)  # six log bins across 1-10 mmag
   105	        return f"amp_ladder_{np.searchsorted(edges, amp_mmag, side='right')}"
   106	    return "amp_lt1"
   107	
   108	
   109	def main() -> None:
   110	    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)
   111	    parser.add_argument("--out-dir", type=Path,
   112	                        default=REPO_ROOT / "generalization/data/d3")
   113	    parser.add_argument("--total", type=int, default=3000)
   114	    parser.add_argument("--mag-cut", type=float, default=13.2)
   115	    args = parser.parse_args()
   116	
   117	    assert_frozen()
   118	    raw_dir = args.out_dir / "raw"
   119	    raw_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
   120	    provenance: dict[str, dict] = {}
   121	
   122	    murphy = cached_pull(raw_dir, "murphy2019_table1.csv", provenance)
   123	    freqs = cached_pull(raw_dir, "mo2026_table2.csv", provenance)
   124	    snf = cached_pull(raw_dir, "mo2026_table1.csv", provenance)
   125	
   126	    if len(murphy) != 14330:
   127	        raise SystemExit(f"Murphy table has {len(murphy)} rows, expected 14330")
   128	    if len(freqs) != 259883:
   129	        raise SystemExit(f"Mo table2 has {len(freqs)} rows, expected 259883")
   130	    if len(snf) != 15265:
   131	        raise SystemExit(f"Mo table1 has {len(snf)} rows, expected 15265")
   132	
   133	    dominant = freqs.loc[freqs.groupby("KIC")["Amp"].idxmax()]
   134	    dominant = dominant.rename(columns={"Freq": "dom_freq_uhz", "Amp": "dom_amp_ppt"})
   135	    subhour_kics = set(snf.loc[snf["C"] == 0, "KIC"].astype(int))
   136	
   137	    stars = murphy.merge(dominant[["KIC", "dom_freq_uhz", "dom_amp_ppt"]], on="KIC", how="left")
   138	    stars["amp_mmag"] = stars["dom_amp_ppt"] * PPT_TO_MMAG
   139	    stars["dom_freq_per_day"] = stars["dom_freq_uhz"] * UHZ_TO_PER_DAY
   140	    stars["subhour"] = stars["KIC"].astype(int).isin(subhour_kics)
   141	    stars = stars[stars["gmag"] >= args.mag_cut].copy()
   142	    if (stars["_DE"] < -28.0).any():
   143	        raise SystemExit("targets below the ZTF footprint; Kepler field expected")
   144	
   145	    positives = stars[stars["dSct"] == 1].sort_values("KIC")
   146	    ambiguous = stars[stars["dSct"] == 2].sort_values("KIC")
   147	    negatives_pool = stars[stars["dSct"] == 0].sort_values("KIC").reset_index(drop=True)
   148	    n_negatives = max(0, args.total - len(positives) - len(ambiguous))
   149	    # frozen-seed simple random sample (G1 referee finding 15: KIC-order stride
   150	    # correlates with sky position/coverage); inclusion probability recorded so
   151	    # population rates can be reweighted
   152	    rng = np.random.Generator(np.random.PCG64(NEGATIVE_SAMPLE_SEED))
   153	    chosen = np.sort(rng.choice(len(negatives_pool), size=n_negatives, replace=False))
   154	    negatives = negatives_pool.iloc[chosen]
   155	
   156	    roster = pd.concat([positives, ambiguous, negatives], ignore_index=True)
   157	    roster["source_id"] = [campaign_id_for_kic(k) for k in roster["KIC"]]
   158	    roster["external_id"] = ["KIC " + str(int(k)) for k in roster["KIC"]]
   159	    roster["ra"] = roster["_RA"]
   160	    roster["dec"] = roster["_DE"]
   161	    roster["class_label"] = ["dsct_flag" + str(int(f)) for f in roster["dSct"]]
   162	    roster["label_variable"] = roster["dSct"].map({0: False, 1: True, 2: None})
   163	    roster["label_periodic"] = roster["label_variable"]
   164	    roster["near_saturation"] = roster["gmag"] < 14.0
   165	    roster["sampling_weight"] = [
   166	        (len(negatives_pool) / len(negatives)) if flag == 0 else 1.0
   167	        for flag in roster["dSct"]
   168	    ]
   169	    roster["stratum"] = [
   170	        amp_ladder_stratum(a, s) if flag == 1 else f"class_{flag}"
   171	        for a, s, flag in zip(roster["amp_mmag"], roster["subhour"], roster["dSct"])
   172	    ]
   173	    bad = [sid for sid in roster["source_id"] if not campaign_id_ok(sid)]
   174	    if bad:
   175	        raise SystemExit(f"generated invalid campaign ids: {bad[:3]}")
   176	    if roster["source_id"].duplicated().any():
   177	        raise SystemExit("duplicate campaign ids")
   178	
   179	    columns = [
   180	        "source_id", "external_id", "ra", "dec", "class_label",
   181	        "label_variable", "label_periodic", "gaia_g_mag",
   182	        "KIC", "gmag", "Teff", "logg", "dSct", "dom_freq_uhz",
   183	        "dom_freq_per_day", "dom_amp_ppt", "amp_mmag", "subhour",
   184	        "near_saturation", "stratum", "sampling_weight",
   185	    ]
   186	    roster["gaia_g_mag"] = ""
   187	    roster_path = args.out_dir / "roster_d3.csv"
   188	    roster[columns].to_csv(roster_path, index=False)
   189	
   190	    pos_amp = positives["amp_mmag"]
   191	    report = {
   192	        "roster": str(roster_path),
   193	        "mag_cut": args.mag_cut,
   194	        "counts": {
   195	            "total": len(roster),
   196	            "positives_dsct1": len(positives),
   197	            "ambiguous_dsct2": len(ambiguous),
   198	            "negatives_dsct0": len(negatives),
   199	            "negatives_pool": len(negatives_pool),
   200	            "negative_sample_seed": NEGATIVE_SAMPLE_SEED,
   201	            "negative_inclusion_probability": n_negatives / len(negatives_pool),
   202	        },
   203	        "positives_amplitude_mmag": {
   204	            "with_amplitude": int(np.isfinite(pos_amp).sum()),
   205	            "without_amplitude": int((~np.isfinite(pos_amp)).sum()),
   206	            "gt10": int((pos_amp > 10).sum()),
   207	            "1to10": int(((pos_amp >= 1) & (pos_amp <= 10)).sum()),
   208	            "lt1": int((pos_amp < 1).sum()),
   209	            "subhour": int(positives["subhour"].sum()),
   210	            "quantiles": {
   211	                q: round(float(np.nanquantile(pos_amp, float(q))), 3)
   212	                for q in ("0.05", "0.25", "0.5", "0.75", "0.95")
   213	            },
   214	        },
   215	        "strata": roster["stratum"].value_counts().to_dict(),
   216	        "provenance": provenance,
   217	        "conversions": {"ppt_to_mmag": PPT_TO_MMAG, "uhz_to_per_day": UHZ_TO_PER_DAY,
   218	                        "kepler_lc_nyquist_uhz": KEPLER_LC_NYQUIST_UHZ},
   219	    }
   220	    (args.out_dir / "roster_report.json").write_text(
   221	        json.dumps(report, indent=2) + "\n", encoding="utf-8"
   222	    )
   223	    print(json.dumps({k: report[k] for k in ("counts", "positives_amplitude_mmag")}, indent=2))
   224	
   225	
   226	if __name__ == "__main__":
   227	    main()

