     1	# METRICS_SPEC — frozen before any campaign Lomb-Scargle run
     2	
     3	Implemented by `scripts/generalization/metrics_generalization.py`. Any change
     4	after the first campaign L-S run voids the prespecification and must be
     5	reported as such. Revised at G1 (2026-08-28) in response to the sol review
     6	panel — see `generalization/reviews/G1/RESPONSE.md`; frozen at G2.
     7	
     8	## Estimand vocabulary (names are binding)
     9	
    10	The campaign does NOT produce a single pooled "selection function". It
    11	produces three separate response assessments with these named estimands:
    12	
    13	- **detection completeness** — P(rule fires | labeled positive), per dataset,
    14	  class, pass rule. D3 denominator: all 610 dSct=1 (external labels).
    15	  D2 denominator: injection targets (synthetic positives — reported as
    16	  *conditional injection-recovery efficiency of the search stage*, never as
    17	  real-sky completeness).
    18	- **frequency-recovery completeness** — P(rule fires AND strict frequency
    19	  match | labeled positive AND frequency-scorable). D3 frequency-scorable:
    20	  the 456/610 with Mo+2026 rows (reported as "Mo-join-conditioned"; joined
    21	  vs unjoined covariates compared). D2: targets with >=1 injected mode
    22	  inside the pass's search bounds after sinc rejection (S_p = 1).
    23	  The missed-vs-wrong-frequency decomposition uses ONLY matching
    24	  denominators (both conditional on scorable/S_p = 1).
    25	- **correct-frequency fraction among detected positives** — what an earlier
    26	  draft called "purity"; it is not positive predictive value and is never
    27	  labeled purity. Class-level PPV is reported for D3 only, with sampling
    28	  weights (negatives carry weight pool/sample = 7292/2314), as a
    29	  prevalence-weighted estimate with the contaminated-negative caveat.
    30	- **negative-class trigger rate** — P(rule fires | Murphy dSct=0). NOT called
    31	  FPR: the class contains non-dSct variables; reported with sampling weights
    32	  and, after adjudication of triggered negatives (W4), split into
    33	  "plausible real variable" vs "unexplained".
    34	- **Gaussian-null false-alarm rate (FPR_Gaussian)** — P(confirmed | arm-A
    35	  zero-amplitude null), n = 1000 over the 928-window frame (windows repeat,
    36	  seeds do not). Acceptance criterion (preregistered): one-sided 95% upper
    37	  bound <= 0.5% at zero events. The FP frequency-distribution/alias audit is
    38	  descriptive only below 10 events.
    39	- **native trigger rate of the template pool** — P(confirmed | paired
    40	  uninjected control window), the 95-prefix arm. Context for D2 recovery,
    41	  not an FPR.
    42	
    43	## Frequency-match taxonomy (disjoint labels, strict first)
    44	
    45	Tolerance: 1.5 / baseline_days per star (the pipeline's own convention) plus
    46	a dataset truth-quantum term for truth-table rounding: D1 +0.0025 / d
    47	(literature frequencies tabulated to 2 decimals), D2/D3 +0 (exact / 6-decimal
    48	uHz). D1 truth frequencies are additionally NON-CONTEMPORANEOUS single-epoch
    49	tabulations of multi-mode pulsators (observed lit-vs-ZTF offsets reach 0.6%),
    50	so D1 frequency-recovery is reported as a DIAGNOSTIC only; D1's estimand is
    51	detection completeness. D1 labels come from the published master table
    52	(19 usable stars; 13 paper-variable, 5 paper-constant) with the frozen
    53	pipeline's eclipsing sanity control (2833849800205759360) excluded as class
    54	`transit_control` — it is a known variable and can serve neither class.
    55	Validation on record (2026-08-28): metrics_generalization on the published
    56	bundle reproduces all five published D1 numbers (11/13 L-S, 9/13 census,
    57	13/13 union, 0 confirmed + 1 candidate among 5 constants).
    58	For each detected candidate, in precedence order against the truth list
    59	(D3: Mo frequencies for that KIC; D2: injected modes):
    60	
    61	1. `direct` — within tolerance of a truth frequency;
    62	2. `harmonic` — within tolerance of 2f or f/2 of a truth frequency;
    63	3. `window_alias` — within tolerance of |f_truth ± k f_sid|, k = 1, 2
    64	   (sidereal-day family, the pipeline's own alias model);
    65	4. `ambiguous` — matches >1 truth frequency class above;
    66	5. `unmatched`.
    67	
    68	Headline frequency recovery counts `direct` only, scored against the
    69	pipeline's BEST candidate (`matched_primary`). D3's primary truth frequency
    70	is the DOMINANT Mo mode; any-mode direct matches are a secondary column.
    71	`matched_any_mode` over the 15 stored top_peaks is diagnostic only.
    72	Chance-match calibration: truth lists permuted across stars (frozen seed,
    73	100 permutations) → accidental direct-match rate reported beside every
    74	frequency-recovery table.
    75	
    76	## Detection rules (all four always reported; PRIMARY = rule 1)
    77	
    78	1. `confirmed` (headline), 2. `confirmed|candidate`, 3. `census`
    79	(any of six frozen ratios >= 2.5), 4. `either` (1 OR 3).
    80	Primary claim family (preregistered): rule 1, pass = best of {low, high}
    81	(the frozen `overall_result` ordering), nominal D2 variant (1.7/0.80,
    82	de-dilution off, arm B), per dataset. Everything else is labeled a
    83	pointwise descriptive sensitivity analysis; no simultaneous-coverage claim.
    84	
    85	## Units of analysis and intervals
    86	
    87	- D1/D3: the star is the unit; Wilson 95% intervals on independent per-star
    88	  proportions; weighted estimates use the effective-sample-size Wilson
    89	  approximation.
    90	- D2: the TESS target is the CLUSTER. K=3 template windows and ladder/phase
    91	  variants are correlated replicates, never pooled as independent trials.
    92	  Per-stratum (10/50/90th percentile window) proportions are reported
    93	  separately; aggregates are equal-weight standardized means over targets
    94	  with cluster bootstrap intervals (resample targets, keep all replicates;
    95	  B = 2000, frozen seed). Ladder results: nominal is primary; the min-max
    96	  across the 3x3 grid is a "prespecified finite-grid sensitivity range",
    97	  never a confidence band; endpoint scenarios identified.
    98	
    99	## Complementarity (census vs L-S)
   100	
   101	Primary table (per dataset, on labeled positives with both methods
   102	available): C = census flag; L = rule-1 detection (detection-only, no
   103	frequency requirement — symmetric margins). Report the full 2x2, both
   104	discordant fractions, union completeness, and incremental yields
   105	P(C=1,L=0), P(C=0,L=1) with intervals (Wilson for D3/D1; cluster bootstrap
   106	for D2). Exact McNemar is SECONDARY (marginal-homogeneity only; it does not
   107	measure complementarity).
   108	
   109	## Surfaces
   110	
   111	Completeness on (log P, log A) and (median exposures-per-night, log A).
   112	Amplitude axis is INVARIANT per dataset: D3 = historical Kepler-band
   113	dominant amplitude (mmag; explicitly non-contemporaneous, not a ZTF-g
   114	threshold); D2 = published TESS amplitude (ppt) for cross-variant surfaces,
   115	nominal injected A_g for the nominal-only surface. Bin edges frozen here:
   116	log P edges at P = {100 s, 200 s, 500 s, 1000 s, 2000 s, 0.05 d, 0.2 d,
   117	1 d, 10 d, 100 d}; amplitude edges {0.5, 1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 50, 200} mmag
   118	(D3) / {0.5, 2, 5, 10, 30, 100} ppt (D2); cells below 5 stars reported as
   119	counts only, no proportion.
   120	
   121	## Eligibility and attrition
   122	
   123	Two denominators, both always reported: P(rule | eligible roster target) and
   124	P(rule | usable light curve) (frozen QC crossmatch passed, both passes
   125	available). A full attrition table (roster -> fetched -> crossmatched ->
   126	QC-passed -> both-passes-complete) by class, amplitude stratum, and
   127	magnitude accompanies every dataset. Unavailable passes are never silently
   128	dropped.
   129	
   130	## Guards
   131	
   132	- Assert no campaign census ratio equals 2.5 exactly.
   133	- Assert every scored JSON has complete == true; both passes present.
   134	- Manifest: SHA-256 of every input file, env versions, frozen + campaign
   135	  file SHAs (frozen_api.campaign_file_shas), replay attestation reference,
   136	  spec git blob SHA.
   137	
   138	## Outputs
   139	
   140	`generalization/results/<date>_<dataset>/metrics/`: per_star.csv,
   141	completeness_by_class_pass_rule.csv, contingency_complementarity.json,
   142	trigger_rates.csv, fp_frequency_distribution.csv, chance_match.csv,
   143	surfaces/*.csv, sensitivity.csv, attrition.csv, manifest.json.
   144	Figures via plot_generalization.py from these CSVs only.

